## Decisions and Action Items

* **Decision**: Drop the `do not explode` flag from [draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec/).
* **Decision**: Adopt composite signatures (MLDSA + Ed25519) directly within [draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec/) as the standard post-quantum cryptographic mechanism.
* **Action Item**: Richard Clayton to publish `-07` of [draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-dkim-dkim2-spec/) including:
  * Clarifying text requiring the initial signature ($I=1$) to align with the RFC 5322 `From` header, alongside multi-signature ordering rules.
  * The Base64 fallback mechanism for handling non-UTF-8 characters in JSON recipes.
  * The removal of the `do not explode` flag.
* **Action Item**: Murray Kucherawy to issue a Call for Adoption (CFA) for `draft-gondwana-dkim2-authres` on the working group mailing list.
* **Action Item**: Bron Gondwana and Wei Chuang to draft a mailing list write-up comparing the sender-side and receiver-side DMARC capabilities lookup scenarios for DKIM2 transition.

